"""A single `simple lint <file>` run must not re-open the same package
`__init__.spl` once per import site.

Measured 2026-09-13 (SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=interpret -- the default JIT lane
segfaults on `lint` when the invoked binary's own path is inside cwd's tree,
filed by PERF-5: doc/08_tracking/bug/lint_default_lane_segfault_from_worktree_bin_path_2026-09-13.md)
on `bin/simple lint test/05_perf/fixtures/interpreter_startup/hello.spl`:

| path                                    | opens (before) | call site |
|------------------------------------------|---:|---|
| `variants/__init__.spl`                   | 76 | `module_resolver::var_overlay::compute_var_roots`, called from `interpreter_module::path_resolution::resolve_module_path_uncached` once per unresolved-import resolution attempt |
| `fix/rules/impl_/__init__.spl`            | 28-29 | `pipeline::module_loader::load_module_with_imports_internal`, recursing once per submodule imported from that package |

Both were attributed with gdb breakpoints on the real glibc `open64`
functions (`__libc_open64` / `__GI___open64_nocancel`), printing a backtrace
on every hit whose pathname argument matched -- `strace -k` is not available
on this host's strace build, and manual Rust-ABI register decoding of the
`read_trace::rts` wrapper's arguments was unreliable, so this is the ground
truth, not a guess:

* `variants/__init__.spl`: the DEPLOYED seed binary's `compute_var_roots` is
  fully inlined with NO cache check (confirmed by disassembling
  `simple_compiler::module_resolver::var_overlay::compute_var_roots` in the
  deployed `bin/simple` -- it goes straight from function entry to
  `Path::join`/`read_to_string`, no thread-local HashMap lookup at all) even
  though the CURRENT SOURCE at this worktree's base (`d522cc98da2`) already
  has `VAR_ROOTS_CACHE`, a thread-local memo landed by an earlier lane
  (`git log` on `var_overlay.rs` shows `8533c416681`/`7bb5ef796a6`, both
  ancestors of this worktree's HEAD). This is a STALE DEPLOYED BINARY, not a
  live source bug -- redeploying the seed from current source fixes this
  target with no further code change. See
  doc/08_tracking/bug/deployed_seed_binary_missing_var_roots_cache_fix_2026-09-13.md.

* `fix/rules/impl_/__init__.spl`: a REAL, present-day source bug, fixed in
  this change. `load_module_with_imports_internal`'s de-dup
  (`if flatten_imports && !visited.insert(path.clone())`) only fires when
  `flatten_imports` is true. A plain (non-glob, non-nested-flatten) member
  import recurses with `flatten_imports=false` for the imported module, which
  skips that check entirely and falls straight through to a fresh
  `fs::read_to_string` -- so a package `__init__.spl` imported by many
  sibling submodules (as `lint_checks.spl`'s dependency tree does here) is
  re-read from disk once per submodule, never memoized. Fixed by
  `MODULE_SOURCE_TEXT_CACHE`, a small per-process thread-local memo of the
  CRLF-normalized raw source text keyed by the already-canonicalized path
  (`src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/pipeline/module_loader.rs`), consulted
  regardless of `flatten_imports`. It caches only the raw text, not the
  parsed+capability-validated `Module`, so a call with a different
  `target_arch` (cfg-stripping is per-call, after the cache) or different
  `importing_capabilities` is unaffected -- byte-identical parse/validate
  behaviour, one fewer disk read.

Re-measured on this lane's own candidate binary (built from this fix,
`src/compiler_rust/target/release/simple`, sha256 `31b41c306aa9...`):
`variants/__init__.spl` 76 -> **1** (confirms the stale-binary theory --
`var_overlay.rs` was not touched by this change); `fix/rules/impl_/__init__.spl`
28-29 -> **2**, stable across repeated runs. The residual 2 is NOT this
function still leaking -- a second gdb pass shows the two opens are two
DIFFERENT PATH SPELLINGS of the same physical, symlinked directory
(`src/compiler/tools` -> `90.tools`): one open of
`.../90.tools/fix/rules/impl_/__init__.spl` through this fix's cache
(`pipeline::module_loader::load_module_with_imports_internal`), one open of
`.../compiler/tools/fix/rules/impl_/__init__.spl` (the symlink spelling,
uncanonicalized) through the INTERPRETER's separate cross-lane cache
(`module_cache::shared_source`). That is a pre-existing, larger, cross-lane
duplication (the same class `PARSED_SOURCE_CACHE`'s own doc comment already
describes for the lowerer/interpreter pair) and is out of scope here -- see
the bug record for the full backtraces.

This spec's `fix/rules/impl_/__init__.spl` row must be at or under budget on
ANY correctly-fixed binary (seed or self-hosted, this worktree's private
candidate or a later official redeploy). The `variants/__init__.spl` row is
recorded for visibility but is NOT gated here -- gating it would fail on
every OFFICIAL deployed binary until whoever owns the redeploy schedule
actually redeploys, which is a deploy-cadence fact, not a code defect this
lane introduced or can fix by editing a `.spl`/`.rs` file. See the two bug
records above for the full split.

Fails closed: an strace that captured nothing, or a count that did not
parse, is a FAIL, not a pass.
"""

use std.spec.*
use std.io_runtime.{process_run}

val FIXTURE: text = "test/05_perf/fixtures/interpreter_startup/hello.spl"

# `fix/rules/impl_/__init__.spl` measured 28-29 opens before this lane's fix,
# 2 after (stable across repeated runs on the candidate binary) -- the
# residual 2 is a documented, separate, cross-lane path-spelling duplication
# (see this file's header), not this function still leaking. The ceiling
# gives headroom above the measured 2 for that residual plus a little slack,
# while still catching a real regression back toward "once per submodule"
# (28-29).
val IMPL_INIT_OPEN_CEILING: i64 = 6

fn run_sh(command: text) -> (text, i64):
    val result = process_run("sh", ["-c", command])
    (result.0 + result.1, result.2)

fn parse_field(blob: text, key: text) -> i64:
    for token in blob.split(" "):
        if token.starts_with(key + "="):
            return token.substring(key.len() + 1, token.len()).trim().to_i64()
    -1

describe "lint's repeated package-__init__.spl opens":
    it "does not re-open fix/rules/impl_/__init__.spl once per submodule import":
        step("strace a lint run under the interpreter lane (the default lane segfaults here)")
        val script = "tmp=$(mktemp -d); b=$SIMPLE_BINARY; "
            + "test -n \"$b\" || b=bin/simple; "
            + "SIMPLE_EXECUTION_MODE=interpret strace -f -e trace=openat -o $tmp/tr "
            + "$b lint " + FIXTURE + " >/dev/null 2>&1; "
            + "echo tracelines=$(wc -l < $tmp/tr) "
            + "variants=$(grep -c 'variants/__init__[.]spl' $tmp/tr) "
            + "impl_init=$(grep -c 'fix/rules/impl_/__init__[.]spl' $tmp/tr); "
            + "rm -rf $tmp"
        val (out, _code) = run_sh(script)
        expect(out.len()).to_be_greater_than(0)
        step("fail closed when strace captured nothing")
        val trace_lines = parse_field(out, "tracelines")
        expect(trace_lines).to_be_greater_than(0)
        step("budget: fix/rules/impl_/__init__.spl")
        val impl_init_opens = parse_field(out, "impl_init")
        expect(impl_init_opens).to_be_greater_than(0)
        expect(impl_init_opens).to_be_less_than(IMPL_INIT_OPEN_CEILING)
